Package: sdgr
Title: Synthetic Datasets from a YAML Config with the 'sdg' Tool
Version: 0.14.0
Authors@R:
    person("William", "Guesdon", email = "wguesdon@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Calls the 'sdg' command line tool from R. The functions write a
    config from a data frame, check a config, generate synthetic data and read
    the synthetic tables back as data frames. The glimpse and the report of a
    data frame hold no real value, so they can leave a secure machine.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Imports:
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    arrow,
    readxl,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: sdg 0.14.0 or later (the Python package of
    https://github.com/wguesdon/synthetic-data-generator)
